Otto,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on wind farms=
, reserves and remote sites; we don't sell packages.

On a wind farm the network question is resilience: when the fibre is cut or s=
tolen, does SCADA stay up, can the O&M crews still work across the site, and =
are the perimeter cameras still reporting? A standby wireless path that takes=
 over automatically costs far less than a day of lost visibility. We have don=
e this kind of work at Oya Wind Farm and at Eskom Medupi.

I've copied Nico as asset manager, since this sits between site operations an=
d the asset.

We've done a desktop terrain study of Jeffreys Bay Wind Farm from 30 m satell=
ite elevation data and the mapped positions of all 60 turbines and the substa=
tion. It's attached, one page, no pricing. What it found:

- Two high sites, one at about 380 m on the western ridge and one at about 17=
0 m in the east, 7.9 km apart with a clear path between them.
- From those two sites, 59 of the 60 turbines are in direct line of sight, an=
d the substation is 3.6 km from the eastern site on a clear path.
- A mapped communications mast 2.0 km from the western site gives a short can=
didate uplink; its operator isn't tagged in the public data, so that's the fi=
rst thing to confirm.
- About 76% of the 85 km2 study area is in line of sight of the two sites.

Those positions are desktop candidates until we walk them. What the study say=
s is that a standby backbone for the whole site needs two masts, not a networ=
k of them.

The next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you have, what fails, wh=
at it costs you when the fibre goes, and what an owned standby path would loo=
k like. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against the build, and the report is yours ei=
ther way. If you can tell me how often the fibre has been cut in the last two=
 years and how long SCADA was blind each time, I'll size the standby path to =
match.

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

